          {
            "id": 2909043,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "In today's class, I'm going to talk about marine archaeology, the branch of archaeology focusing on the human interaction with the sea, lakes, and rivers. It's the study of ships, cargoes, shipping facilities, and other physical remains. I'll give you an example, then go on to show how this type of research is being transformed by the use of the latest technology. Atlityan was a village on the coast of the Eastern Mediterranean, which seems to have been thriving until around 7,000 BC. The residents kept cattle, caught fish, and stored grain.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2909044,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "In today's class, I'm going to talk about marine archaeology, the branch of archaeology focusing on the human interaction with the sea, lakes, and rivers.",
