                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2909242,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "It's been described as the largest and best preserved prehistoric settlement ever found on the seabed. For marine archaeologists, Atlit Yam is a treasure trove. Research on the buildings, tools, and the human remains has revealed how the bustling village once functioned and even what diseases some of its residents suffered from. But, of course, this is only one small village, one window into a lost world. For a fuller picture, researchers need more sunken settlements, but the hard part is finding them.",
            "children": [
              {
