                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2909313,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "For a fuller picture, researchers need more sunken settlements, but the hard part is finding them.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 221.535,
                  "from": 213.535,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2909330,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Underwater research used to require divers to find shipwrecks or artifacts. But in the second half of the twentieth century, various types of underwater vehicles were developed, some controlled from a ship on the surface and some of them autonomous, which means they don't need to be operated by a person. Autonomous underwater vehicles or AUVs are used in the oil industry, for instance, to create maps of the seabed before rigs and pipelines are installed. To navigate, they use sensors such as compasses and sonar. Until relatively recently, they were very expensive and so heavy that they had to be launched from a large vessel with a winch.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2909331,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Underwater research used to require divers to find shipwrecks or artifacts.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 229.50002,
                  "from": 223.5,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2909343,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "But in the second half of the twentieth century, various types of underwater vehicles were developed, some controlled from a ship on the surface and some of them autonomous, which means they don't need to be operated by a person.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 245.37502,
                  "from": 229.74,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2909384,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Autonomous underwater vehicles or AUVs are used in the oil industry, for instance, to create maps of the seabed before rigs and pipelines are installed.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 259.91998,
                  "from": 246.815,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2909410,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "To navigate, they use sensors such as compasses and sonar.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 267.11502,
                  "from": 261.275,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2909421,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Until relatively recently, they were very expensive and so heavy that they had to be launched from a large vessel with a winch.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 276.875,
                  "from": 267.915,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2909445,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "But the latest AUVs are much easier to maneuver. They can be launched from the shore or a small ship, and they're much cheaper, which makes them more accessible to research teams. They are also very sophisticated. They can communicate with each other and, for example, work out the most efficient way to survey a site or to find particular objects on the seabed. Field tests show the approach can work.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2909446,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "But the latest AUVs are much easier to maneuver.",
                "meta": {
